      "body": "## Summary\n- Add `VLLM_ALLOW_INSUFFICIENT_KV_CACHE` as an expert-only startup override.\n- Keep the default hard failure when max_model_len does not fit the estimated KV cache budget.\n- When explicitly enabled, downgrade only that capacity failure to a detailed warning and continue.\n- Preserve the hard failure for `available_memory <= 0`.\n\nRefs #50509\n\n## Test Plan\n- `pytest tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py::test_allow_insufficient_kv_cache_downgrades_capacity_error tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py::test_allow_insufficient_kv_cache_does_not_ignore_empty_cache -q`\n- `python -m ruff check vllm/envs.py vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py`\n- `python -m py_compile vllm/envs.py vllm/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py`\n- `git diff --check`",
